 lines=[f'# TIC {tic}: {verdicts[tic]}', '',reasons[tic], '',f'Full-review completion: COMPLETE (adjudicated). Novelty: no prior target EB classification found in successful queried catalogues; limited prior-art coverage, not a guaranteed discovery claim. Current SIMBAD identifies {a["simbad"][0]["main_id"]} as {a["simbad"][0]["otype"]}; known spectroscopic binarity is distinct from prior eclipse classification.', '', '## Raw SAP, individual events and ephemerides','',f'{len(ev)} accepted primary fits across {len(set(e["sec"] for e in ev))} sectors; median depth {depth*1000:.3f} ppt. Shared exposure-integrated trapezoid T14={r["shape"]["T14"]*24:.4f} h, profile range {np.array(r["shape"]["T14_range"])*24} h; fractional ingress={r["shape"]["fr"]:.3f}. T12 and T23 below are trapezoid coordinates; a grazing flat segment is not physical totality.', '',eptext(ep),'',f'Secondary: {s["statistic"]["n"]} usable windows, {s["statistic"]["n_individual_gt3sigma"]} individual >3σ; combined depth {s["statistic"]["depth"]*1000:.4f} ± {s["statistic"]["empirical_error"]*1000:.4f} ppt (event-scatter error). Fitted phase={phase:.7f}, Gaia nominal={s["predicted_gaia_phase"]:.7f}. Phase was optimized; repeatability and controls matter more than its single-trial S/N.','',eptext(s['ephemeris']),'',table(['kind','sector','mid BTJD ± d','depth ± ppt','T14/T12/T23 h','β','O−C min'],[[kind,e['sec'],f"{e['tc']:.7f} ± {e['tc_error']:.3g}",f"{e['depth']*1000:.3f} ± {e['depth_error']*1000:.3f}",'/'.join(f"{e[k]*24:.3f}" for k in ('T14','T12','T23')),fmt(e['beta']),fmt(e.get('oc_days',0)*1440)] for kind,events in [('P',ev),('S',se)] for e in events]),'',f'All primary timing scans interior: {not any(e["scan_edge"] for e in ev)}. QUALITY=0 fits retain all untrimmed cadences; {sum(e["flagged_core"] for e in ev)} flagged core cadences inspected separately in event records. Minimum background-regressed/ordinary primary depth ratio={bgmin:.4f}; background is standardized in native units, never divided by normalized SAP. Centroid template shifts/errors are retained per event in fit-results.json and are not by themselves source localization.', '',f'Blind rolling-median census: {len(r["census"])} triggers; {len(off)} outside the two eclipse phase windows. Largest off-phase dip={max([x["depth"] for x in off],default=0)*1000:.3f} ppt, versus primary median {depth*1000:.3f} ppt. No off-phase event of comparable primary depth. Off-phase s094 triggers cluster near the known 3875 BTJD sector systematic where applicable; shallow isolated census triggers are not additional classified eclipses. Full trigger/threshold/duration list and every rejected/insufficient event window remain in fit-results.json; coverage failures are not nulls.', '', '## Own Gaia covariance and physical interpretation','',f'Source {t["gaia"]["source_id"]}; covariance bit_index={o["gaia_bit_index"]}; source and SB1/SB2 layout asserted before reconstruction. Photometric period minus Gaia period={o["period_delta_sigma"]:.3f}σ. Primary matches conjunction {o["primary_conjunction"]}. Per-event Gaia predictions, correlated timing errors and residuals are in orbit-gates.json; no correlation copied from another source.','', '```json',json.dumps(dict(gaia_primary_epoch_comparison=[{k:v for k,v in z.items() if k!='events'} for z in o['gaia_comparison']],eccentricity_comparison=cv,physics=o['physics'],shape_feasibility=g),indent=2),'```','', 'Physical quantities using TIC primary properties and approximate companion radii are conditional feasibility checks. The mass function and minimum mass establish stellar-scale companions; main-sequence radii are not measured constraints. A/B conjunction uses Gaia primary ω without a 180° change. Two-disk models use limb darkening and partial overlap; no e sinω is inferred by treating a grazing trapezoid T23 as totality. Free depth scales, grid boundaries, χ² and dilution prevent precise radii/mass-ratio claims.','']
 if (p/'null-secondary.json').exists():lines += ['The other-conjunction covariance/width-tested pointwise limits are retained below. Every individual clean/flagged/insufficient window is retained in null-secondary.json. These are conditional pointwise limits, not a simultaneous confidence envelope; fitted coverage uses actual clean cadences.', '', '```json',json.dumps(nullsummary(p/'null-secondary.json'),indent=2),'```','']
